  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 210 PM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nEnsembles continue to suggest the central Plains ridge strengthens \nand advances eastward on Saturday. This will bring in heat by \nSaturday afternoon, and even warmer temperatures Sunday. \nTemperatures near 90 appear likely Saturday, and perhaps mid 90s by \nSunday. Tropical storm Bertha will be nothing more than a breeze by \nthe weekend and should allow for an open gulf moisture stream. \nEvapotranspiration is also near its peak at this point in the \nsummer. At this time, it looks like dewpoints will rise to at least \nthe mid 70s. This would adjust apparent temps up by several degrees \nand give us potential for 100+ heat indices Saturday through Monday \nin some locations. The position of the ridge and fairly strong mid-\nlevel flow Sunday into early-week will put our area in ring of fire \nposition with potential for several rounds of strong storms. \nHigh instability and potential for a decent nocturnal LLJ makes \nSunday into Monday the current best estimate for the next \nchances at severe weather, but details are unclear at this time.\nThe jet pattern becomes less clear after Monday, and confidence\nin storm chances is low beyond Monday.",
